history/2024-04-bounded-delegation.md-2-
history/2024-04-bounded-delegation.md-3-Status: ARCHIVED.
history/2024-04-bounded-delegation.md-4-Record identifier: rc-202404-04.
history/2024-04-bounded-delegation.md-5-This review record is part of the release-control history. It is intentionally
history/2024-04-bounded-delegation.md:6:detailed because incident response and replay compare decisions across schema
history/2024-04-bounded-delegation.md:7:revisions. Delegation became a first-class constraint. An expired grant is visible to replay and audit, but it is not a current pass. A delegate may not widen the grantor's capability or tenant. The evaluator must keep delegation beside membership rather than replacing membership.
history/2024-04-bounded-delegation.md-8-
history/2024-04-bounded-delegation.md-9-## Reading rule
history/2024-04-bounded-delegation.md-10-
history/2024-04-bounded-delegation.md-11-For a current decision, read the current source path named by the public entry
history/2024-04-bounded-delegation.md-12-point and assemble one frozen snapshot. This record clarifies terminology and
history/2024-04-bounded-delegation.md-13-precedence. It does not replace executable source. An archived record can
history/2024-04-bounded-delegation.md-14-explain why a legacy fixture has a different answer, but it cannot make that
history/2024-04-bounded-delegation.md-15-answer valid for a new request.
--
