history/2024-11-deny-precedence.md-35-
history/2024-11-deny-precedence.md-36-1. A missing input fails closed before a live adapter is queried.
history/2024-11-deny-precedence.md-37-2. A record can be visible in history while being ineligible for a current decision.
history/2024-11-deny-precedence.md:38:3. A false applicable predicate is a denial; it is not equivalent to no predicate.
history/2024-11-deny-precedence.md-39-4. The current snapshot is authoritative for one decision and is never rebuilt halfway through it.
history/2024-11-deny-precedence.md-40-5. A helper name is not a contract: callers must check the actual aggregation and precedence.
history/2024-11-deny-precedence.md-41-6. Archived examples are evidence about an earlier revision, not exceptions to the current rule.
history/2024-11-deny-precedence.md-42-7. Current policy records intentionally keep declaration order for deterministic audit output.
history/2024-11-deny-precedence.md-43-8. The public result is boolean, but the review trace must retain every intermediate reason.
history/2024-11-deny-precedence.md-44-9. A successful early check cannot authorize a request whose later required check fails.
history/2024-11-deny-precedence.md-45-10. The final quota check is a read in this function; reservation is a separate operation.
history/2024-11-deny-precedence.md-46-11. Unknown channels, capabilities, and node kinds are not silently converted to stable defaults.
history/2024-11-deny-precedence.md-47-12. Normalization removes representational differences but never changes policy truth.
