history/2024-08-policy-chains.md-5-This review record is part of the release-control history. It is intentionally
history/2024-08-policy-chains.md:6:detailed because incident response and replay compare decisions across schema
history/2024-08-policy-chains.md:7:revisions. The policy record changed from a single predicate to an ordered chain. Reviewers explicitly chose all-applicable semantics: a request that passes identity but fails region is denied. The old any-of helper was kept for replaying pre-chain records while new decisions use the current contract.
history/2024-08-policy-chains.md-8-
history/2024-08-policy-chains.md-9-## Reading rule
history/2024-08-policy-chains.md-10-
history/2024-08-policy-chains.md-11-For a current decision, read the current source path named by the public entry
history/2024-08-policy-chains.md-12-point and assemble one frozen snapshot. This record clarifies terminology and
history/2024-08-policy-chains.md-13-precedence. It does not replace executable source. An archived record can
history/2024-08-policy-chains.md-14-explain why a legacy fixture has a different answer, but it cannot make that
history/2024-08-policy-chains.md-15-answer valid for a new request.
