history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-41-
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-42-Rows E02, E09, E12, and E24 are especially important. They distinguish
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md:43:"all applicable required constraints" from an any-of shortcut. The fact that a
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-44-friendly node passes does not erase a failed required node. Rows E18-E21
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md:45:distinguish current matching vetoes from historical or nonmatching records.
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-46-Rows E07, E15, and E23 distinguish a catalog miss or stale revision from a
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-47-published rule.
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-48-
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-49-A reviewer must not infer behavior from the result column alone. The source
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-50-path, selected revision, and node applicability still have to be checked.
