history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-52-
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-53-## Stability rules
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-54-
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-55-- Comparisons use integer timestamps and a fixed 24-hour request age.
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-56-- Region and capability aliases are resolved before policy lookup.
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md:57:- Current source wins over an archived fixture when replay and admission are
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-58-  compared.
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-59-- No default stable policy is selected for an unknown capability.
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-60-- No result is true merely because the chain contains at least one passing
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-61-  node.
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md:62:- A deny and a conflict are both final vetoes.
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-63-- Quota availability is observed without mutation by the public function.
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-64-- The output of the public function is a boolean; explanations carry detail.
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-65-
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-66-## Review sign-off
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-67-
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-68-The edge-case suite is accepted only if the current call path agrees with the
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md:69:matrix for every row. In particular, a case with one applicable true node and
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md:70:one applicable false node is denied. This is the current invariant, not a
history/2026-09-edge-case-matrix.md-71-preference and not an interpretation left to the caller.
